:blocked? false :value (get parked' parked-id) :wait-set entries)\n  2267\t            (assoc machine :halted? false :blocked? true :value :yin/blocked :wait-set entries))\n  2268\t          custody kind root?)))))\n  2269\t\n  2270\t\n  2271\t(defn lower-task\n  2272\t  \"The lower of §7.2 into recv, a fresh semantic machine of the\n  2273\t   receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,\n  2274\t   then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,\n  2275\t   primitives), each step over the whole tree before the next, then\n  2276\t   custody (check-custody!), all before the first attach! (step 11); then\n  2277\t   restore (step 12), which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the\n  2278\t   restored machine, or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\n  2279\t   opts: :budget; :yin.k/admitted-modules, a composition-supplied {name manifest-address}\n  2280\t   for carried install children (default empty, fail closed). Name-keyed admission\n  2281\t   is flat over the whole task tree: the same name at different addresses cannot\n  2282\t   be admitted together. The lift never carries sender admission fields; a carried\n  2283\t   one is refused as :yin.k/undecodable :install-response; :exclusive, refuse a fork root; :grant and :protection,\n  2284\t   required by a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's reader\n  2285\t   contract: the grant names :checkpoint, the pack address, its lease,\n  2286\t   holder, tenure and evidence; :protection maps every stream identity of\n  2287\t   the tree to its class); :fenced, an administrative rehydration that\n  2288\t   skips the grant and restores every task of the tree gated :exporting,\n  2289\t   its waits in :yin.k/recovery-waits and its parked records in\n  2290\t   :yin.k/recovery-parked (none in the scheduler), its id counter the\n  2291\t   carried one exactly and :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids mapping each cursor\n  2292\t   cell's resource key to its carried cell