4\t      {:yin.k/hold :link-cursor-not-installed})))\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\t(defn- first-refusal\n   108\t  [vm]\n   109\t  (some (fn [[path m]]\n   110\t          (when (seq (:ready-queue m))\n   111\t            {:yin.k/status :yin.k/not-quiescent\n   112\t             :yin.k/path path\n   113\t             :yin.k/ready (count (:ready-queue m))}))\n   114\t        (machines [] vm)))\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t;; =============================================================================\n   118\t;; Entering exporting\n   119\t;; =============================================================================\n   120\t\n   121\t(defn enter\n   122\t  \"Enter exporting from `machine`.  Answers\n   123\t   `{:status :ok :machine m :record r}`: `m` is `machine` with the gate\n   124\t   `:exporting`, an empty wait set and no parked record, and `r` the\n   125\t   export record, holding the wait set in order, every parked record\n   126\t   (the row carrier carries them all, continuation §2.5), and the gate\n   127\t   to return to.  Otherwise answers the data outcome of the first\n   128\t   refusal, leaving `machine` as it was: `:yin.k/not-quiescent` for\n   129\t   queued work in the root or a child, a `:yin.k/non-portable` of kind\n   130\t   `:reason-mismatch` (naming the hold and the task path), or\n   131\t   `:yin.k/refused` for a machine that is already exporting or ended.\"\n   132\t  [machine]\n   133\t  (cond\n   134\t    (contains? #{:exporting :ended} (vm/gate-mode machine))\n   135\t    (refused :not-running)\n   136\t\n   137\t    :else\n   138\t    (or (first-refusal machine)\n   139\t        (some (fn [[path m]]\n   140\t                (when-some [h (refusal-at m)]\n   141\t                  (non-portable (assoc h :yin.k/path path))))\n   142\t              (machines [] machine))\n   143\t        {:status :ok\n   144\t         :machine (cond-> (assoc machine :yin.k/gate :exporting :wait-set [])\n   145\t                    (contains? machine :parked) (assoc :parked {}))\n   146\t         :record {:wait-set (vec (:wait-set machine))\n   147\t                  :parked (:parked machine)\n   148\t                  :gate (vm/gate-mode machine)\n   149\t                  :served {}}})))\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t(defn- reinstated\n   153\t  \"`machine`, an exporting machine, carrying `record`'s waits and\n   154\t   parked records again: the value the lift reads.\"\n   155\t  [machine record]\n   156\t  (-> (reduce-kv (fn [restored module-name child-record]\n   157\t                   (update-in restored [:installs module-name :vm]\n   158\t                              reinstated child-record))\n   159\t                 machine (or (:children record) {}))\n   160\t      (assoc :wait-set (:wait-set record))\n   270\t      {:status :ok :record (assoc record :served @table)}\n   271\t      (assoc r :record (assoc record :served @table)))))\n   272\t\n   273\t\n   274\t(defn- kind-of\n   275\t  \"The lifted task's kind, by the lift's own rule.\"\n   276\t  [m]\n   277\t  (let [value (:value m)]\n   278\t    (cond\n   279\t      (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value))\n   280\t           (contains? (:parked m) (:id value))) :parked\n   281\t      (seq (:wait-set m)) :blocked\n   282\t      :else :halted)))\n   283\t\n   284\t\n   285\t(defn encode\n   286\t  \"The lift of the prepared `record` over `machine`, from a `serve-keyed`\n   287\t   that only reads the record, under the header and source index the\n   288\t   record retains: `{:status :ok :bytes b :address a :root B :kind k}`,\n   289\t   `b` the pack's canonical bytes, `a` the pack address (BLAKE3 of `b`,\n   290\t   the storage key), `B` the root id inside it; or the lift's refusal as\n   291\t   data.  It allocates and publishes nothing, and one record gives equal\n   292\t   bytes every time.  A stream the record has no answer for is a defect\n   293\t   of the caller (an unprepared record), not a refusal.\"\n   294\t  [machine record]\n   295\t  (let [served (:served record)\n   296\t        r (lift machine record\n   297\t                (fn [k _h]\n   298\t                  (if (contains? served k)\n   299\t                    (get served k)\n   300\t                    (throw (ex-info \"Encode of an unprepared record\"\n   570\t   `transport-error` stays the unknown-delivery refusal, as does no\n   571\t   answer.\"\n   572\t  [outcome]\n   573\t  (contains? #{:dao.stream/full :dao.stream/invalid-value\n   574\t               :dao.stream/closed :dao.stream/refused}\n   575\t             outcome))\n   576\t\n   577\t\n   578\t(defn abort\n   579\t  \"Return the exporting `machine` to local execution from `record`.\n   580\t\n   581\t   `attempts` is the offer-attempt history the composition persisted:\n   582\t   one map per attempt whose intent was durable before the send, with\n   583\t   `:append` the outcome its append answered (absent when none did).\n   584\t   Abort is legal when there is no attempt, or when every attempt's\n   585\t   append proves the value was not appended; anything else, including\n   586\t   an authority's refusal of one attempt, leaves the source fenced.  A\n   587\t   recovered record (`rehydrate-fenced`) is refused `:restarted`: a\n   588\t   restart never hands execution back.\n   589\t\n   590\t   A machine under custody (`:yin.k/custody`) is a holder exporting a\n   591\t   successor: it may abort only with `tenure`, `{:now n :bound b :live\n   592\t   true}`: `n` before `b` in one unit, and `:live` the ledger reader's\n   593\t   evidence that this lease is the occurrence's active lease at its\n   594\t   epoch.  A clock reading alone is not tenure.  After the lease has\n   595\t   ended its old local machine is never restored.\n   596\t\n   597\t   Answers `{:status :ok :machine m}` or `:yin.k/refused` data with\n   598\t   reason `:restarted`, `:not-exporting`, `:tenure-ended` (at or past\n   599\t   the bound), `:tenure-unconfirmed` (no ledger evidence) or\n   600\t   `:offer-possibly-accepted`.\"\n   601\t  [machine record attempts tenure]\n   602\t  (cond\n   603\t    (:recovered? record)\n   604\t    (refused :restarted)\n   605\t\n   606\t    (not= :exporting (vm/gate-mode machine))\n   607\t    (refused :not-exporting)\n   608\t\n   609\t    (and (contains? machine :yin.k/custody)\n   610\t         (some? (:now tenure))\n   611\t         (some? (:bound tenure))\n   612\t         (>= (:now tenure) (:bound tenure)))\n   613\t    (refused :tenure-ended)\n   614\t\n   615\t    (and (contains? machine :yin.k/custody)\n   616\t         (not (and (some? (:now tenure))\n   617\t                   (some? (:bound tenure))\n   618\t                   (true? (:live tenure)))))\n   619\t    (refused :tenure-unconfirmed)\n   620\t\n   120\t       :side-table @side})))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- allocation\n   124\t  [v a {:keys [start end owner]}]\n   125\t  (let [locals (if (nil? owner) 0 (count (nth (nth v owner) 2)))\n   126\t        defined (into #{} (keep #(code/rd (nth v %))) (range start end))\n   127\t        points (reduce (fn [m pc]\n   128\t                         (reduce (fn [m r] (update m r (fnil conj []) pc)) m\n   129\t                                 (into (analysis/live a pc) (analysis/defs v pc))))\n   130\t                       {} (range start end))\n   131\t        intervals (mapv (fn [r] [r (apply min (get points r)) (apply max (get points r))])\n   132\t                        (sort defined))\n   133\t        starts-by-pc (group-by second intervals)\n   134\t        missing (seq (remove defined (mapcat #(code/uses (nth v %)) (range start end))))]\n   135\t    (loop [pc start active [] free (sorted-set) next-slot 0 slots {}]\n   136\t      (if (= pc end)\n   137\t        {:locals locals :registers (+ locals next-slot (if missing 1 0))\n   138\t         :start start :end (dec end)\n   139\t         :slots slots :structural (+ locals next-slot)}\n   140\t        (let [expired (sort-by (juxt #(nth % 2) first)\n   141\t                               (filter #(< (nth % 2) pc) active))\n   142\t              free (into free (map #(get slots (first %))) expired)\n   143\t              active (filterv #(>= (nth % 2) pc) active)\n   144\t              starts (get starts-by-pc pc [])\n   145\t              [free next-slot slots]\n   146\t              (reduce (fn [[free next-slot slots] [r]]\n   147\t                        (let [i (if (seq free) (first free) next-slot)]\n   148\t                          [(disj free i) (if (seq free) next-slot (inc next-slot))\n   149\t                           (assoc slots r i)]))\n   150\t                      [free next-slot slots] starts)]\n   151\t          (recur (inc pc) (into active starts) free next-slot slots))))))\n   152\t\n   153\t\n   154\t(defn register-image\n   155\t  \"Allocate temporaries by linear scan over A's live points; preserve A's\n   156\t   layout and fill saved windows using the register format's liveness.\"\n   157\t  [v]\n   158\t  (let [{rv :vector bodies :bodies} (resolve v)\n   159\t        a (analysis/analyze v)\n   160\t        allocations (mapv #(allocation v a %) bodies)\n   161\t        instructions\n   162\t        (mapv (fn [pc t]\n   163\t                (let [{:keys [slots locals structural]}\n   164\t                      (nth allocations (code/body-index bodies pc))\n   165\t                      physical (fn [r] (if (contains? slots r) (+ locals (get slots r)) structural))\n   166\t                      op (first t)\n   167\t                      fields (get rcode/opcode-table op)]\n   168\t                  (into [op]\n   169\t                        (map-indexed (fn [i [k kind]]\n   170\t                                       (if (= k :yin.debruijn.register/live) []\n   171\t                                           (let [x (nth t (inc i))]\n   172\t                                             (case kind\n   173\t                                               :reg (physical x)\n   174\t                                               :regs (mapv physical x)\n   175\t                                               x)))) fields))))\n   176\t              (range (count rv)) rv)\n   177\t        image {:bodies (mapv #(select-keys % [:locals :registers :start :end]) allocations)\n   178\t               :instructions instructions}]\n   179\t    (reduce (fn [image bi]\n   180\t              (reduce (fn [image [pc live]]\n   181\t                        (assoc-in image [:instructions pc\n   182\t                                         (rcode/live-slot-index (first (nth instructions pc)))] live))\n   183\t                      image (rcode/body-liveness image bi)))\n   184\t            image (range (count bodies)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
